<Step id="STEP_4_HANDOFF">
      <Action>
        Per `AX_HANDOFF_TYPED`, return `HANDOFF_FORMAT` with files changed, requirements demonstrated, commands/results,
        deviations, and the next declared phase. Return the payload in the response only. Do not call
        `sdd-log`, manually edit the ticket, remove its placeholders, or mark any checkbox. The
        orchestrator validates the payload against Git plus the CLI-owned receipt and performs the
        single `sdd-log complete` transition. Do not write JSON checkpoints, worker IDs, session keys,
        or NEXT state.
      </Action>
    </Step>

<Axiom id="AX_HANDOFF_TYPED">
      End every phase block with a typed Handoff line consumed by the next phase and the orchestrator. Format per `HANDOFF_FORMAT`. Free-form text forbidden — the next phase reads keys, not narrative.
    </Axiom>

<Contract id="HANDOFF_FORMAT">
  Compact, typed, single line at end of phase block:
  ```
  **Handoff →** artifacts: [path1, path2]; decisions: [key=value(measured), key=value]; open: [id(reported; depth-only): text, id: text]; deviations: [id: text, id: text]
  ```
  Fields:
  - `artifacts` — files produced or modified by this phase (paths).
  - `decisions` — key facts the next phase or audit needs (e.g. `IdempotencyKey=introduced`,
    `module-system=esm`). Each entry MAY carry a trailing provenance tag
    `key=value(measured|reported|assumed)`: `measured` — this phase directly observed it (ran a
    command, read the file); `reported` — carried verbatim from a prior phase's own Handoff, not
    re-observed; `assumed` — inferred/expected, not directly checked. An untagged entry is
    `assumed` by convention (`ISS-11`) — omitting the tag never upgrades a guess to a fact.
  - `open` — unresolved questions / risks / deferred sub-tasks. Each entry is `id: text` or, when
    its provenance and coverage matter, `id(tag; extent): text` — `tag` is the same
    `measured|reported|assumed` vocabulary, `extent` is one short phrase naming what the item
    actually covers (e.g. `depth-only`, `not coverage`) so a narrowed follow-up cannot be misread
    as covering the whole original question. Empty list → `[]`.
  - `deviations` — spec/ticket holes this phase self-resolved rather than asking the operator
    (`AX_DEVIATION_SELF_RESOLVE`); each entry cites the ticket-local Decision Log id it produced
    (e.g. `TSK-58-D-2: chose retry cap 3, spec silent on it`). Empty list → `[]`.

  Free-form text forbidden outside the tag/extent grammar above. Each field is an array (possibly
  empty).
</Contract>